## Known Limitations & Live Testing Notes

This resource is a `_v1` pilot: schema/model types are generated by
`tfplugingen-framework` from SailPoint's per-service `/service-desk-integrations/v1`
OpenAPI spec, but Create/Read/Update/Delete are hand-written against the
`golang-sdk`'s `api_beta.ServiceDeskIntegrationApi` client. The following was
learned from running `terraform apply`, acceptance tests, and unit tests
against real API/SDK behavior, not just from the spec:

- **`cluster_ref` is effectively required for some connector types**,
  despite the OpenAPI spec only listing `name`/`description`/`type`/
  `attributes` as required. Live testing against a real sandbox tenant showed
  `Create` fails outright for the `ServiceNowSDIM` (and `Generic SDIM`)
  connector `type`s when `cluster_ref` is omitted. Always set `cluster_ref`
  unless you have verified your specific connector type does not need it.
- **Known upstream SDK bug for `provisioning_config.managed_resource_refs`.**
  The vendored `golang-sdk`'s
  `ProvisioningConfigManagedResourceRefsInner.Type/Id/Name` fields are
  mistyped as `map[string]interface{}` instead of `string` (confirmed by
  direct source inspection across multiple SDK releases, not fixed by
  upgrading). This means the SDK itself cannot decode a real API response for
  any service desk integration whose `provisioningConfig.managedResourceRefs`
  is non-empty - `Read`/`Import`/data-source lookups against such an object
  will fail. This provider works around the bug with a raw-JSON fallback
  decode path so a non-empty `managedResourceRefs` doesn't crash the whole
  response; newly created integrations (which always start with an empty
  `managedResourceRefs`) are unaffected.
- **Optional+Computed nested reference blocks must guard `IsUnknown()`,
  not just `IsNull()`, before Create.** `before_provisioning_rule`,
  `cluster_ref`, and `owner_ref` are `Optional+Computed`, so when omitted
  from configuration Terraform sends them as *Unknown* (not *Null*) to
  `Create` - normal Optional+Computed plan behavior. Only `plan`-only
  validation was run for a long time, which never surfaces this because
  `plan` never invokes `Create`; a real acceptance-test `apply` caught it.
